note ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note This file is a specification illustration. It uses record declarations,
note abilities and control flow, which the single file reference front end does
note not implement yet (see spec/15 section 15.8). Programs that the reference
note can compile today are hello.shark, tour*.shark, pages.shark and ambiguity.shark.
note ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

note A neural network, written in the same language as the interface and the
note server. The compiler differentiates the forward pass directly from SIR,
note so a hand written layer is differentiable with no registration step.

use tensor
use model

let vocabulary size be 32000
let width be 512
let depth be 12

create neural network Brain
  an embedding layer of width
  repeat depth times
    an attention layer with 8 heads and width width
    a dense layer of 2048 activated by gelu
  a dense layer of vocabulary size

note --------------------------------------------------------------- training

to train the brain on a corpus
  give Brain training data from corpus
  train Brain
    for 3 epochs
    using adam with learning rate 0.0003

note --------------------------------------------------------------- a custom layer

note Nothing here is special to the framework. It is ordinary Shark over
note tensors, and `train` will differentiate it.

to apply a swiglu to an input with a gate weight and an up weight
  let gated be matrix product of input and gate weight
  let raised be matrix product of input and up weight
  give elementwise multiply over
    elementwise silu over gated
    raised

note --------------------------------------------------------------- inference

when Brain receives text
  run on the gpu
    let answer be ask Brain about the received text
  give answer

note --------------------------------------------------------------- serving it

use net

serve on port 9000
  when a request arrives at /ask isolated
    let question be the body of the request
    let answer be ask Brain about question
    reply with json answer

note ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
note `compose explain transfers` reports every byte that crosses to the GPU and
note where it was elided because the tensor was already resident.
note
note Floating point contraction is off by default inside `run on the gpu`, so the
note device result matches the host result bit for bit. Turn it on per region with
note `allow fused multiply add` when you want the extra speed.
